// PC-side Zenoh client config for when the Mac and Pi are on the SAME local
// network (e.g. NTU Secure, a shared hotspot) instead of reaching each other
// over Tailscale. Same mode:"client" / SHM-disabled setup as
// zenoh_client_pc.json5 — the only difference is the endpoint IP, since a LAN
// DHCP lease won't match the Pi's Tailscale IP.
//
// UPDATE THE IP BELOW each time you join a new LAN: on the Pi, run
// `hostname -I` (or `ip -4 addr show wlan0`) and take its LAN address (the
// 192.168.x.x / 10.x.x.x one — NOT the 100.x.x.x Tailscale address).
//
// If the Pi is unreachable even on the same SSID (ping fails both ways),
// the network likely enforces client/AP isolation and this won't work no
// matter what IP you plug in — fall back to zenoh_client_pc.json5 over
// Tailscale (accepting the DERP-relay throughput penalty) or to a private
// hotspot instead.
{
  mode: "client",
  connect: {
    endpoints: [
      "tcp/192.168.1.100:7447" // <-- REPLACE with the Pi's current LAN IP
    ]
  },
  transport: {
    shared_memory: {
      enabled: false
    }
  }
}
